---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Golf from '../../../Images/golf.png';
import ProjectHero from '../../../components/ProjectHero.astro';
import ProjectSection from '../../../components/ProjectSection.astro';
---

<Layout title="Golf Tracker | Batiste COMET-BARTHE" backHref="/en/#projects" lang="en">
  <ProjectHero
    category="Personal project · Amazfit T-Rex 2 · Connected sports"
    title="Golf"
    accent="Tracker"
    description="An on-course companion for Amazfit watches: GPS positioning, distances to greens and hazards, shot tracking, and hole-by-hole scoring."
    tags={['Zepp OS', 'JavaScript ES5', 'GPS', 'OpenStreetMap', 'Bluetooth']}
    image={Golf}
    imageAlt="Golf tracker screen showing a hole, GPS distances, and the green map"
    technologyLabel="Technologies"
  />

  <section class="px-6 pb-32" style="background: #09090b;">
    <ProjectSection variant="wide">
      <div class="golf-project-content">
        <article class="golf-project-row">
          <h2>01 — The project</h2>
          <div class="golf-project-row__body">
            <p>
              Golf Tracker is a round-tracking app designed for the Amazfit T-Rex 2. The watch’s round screen becomes an at-a-glance on-course dashboard, bringing together a hole map, the player’s GPS position, and useful distances—without needing to take out a phone.
            </p>
            <p>
              The project is built on Zepp OS and its embedded JavaScript environment. A companion phone app rounds out the experience, letting players prepare courses and configure a game.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="golf-project-row">
          <h2>02 — Prepare the course</h2>
          <div class="golf-project-row__body">
            <p>
              From the phone settings, players can search for nearby golf courses using OpenStreetMap data. The companion service queries Overpass, correlates tees, greens, and bunkers, then sends a compact version of the course data to the watch.
            </p>
            <p>
              Backup courses remain available on the watch: a round can start with this local data while a custom course is being searched for or synchronized.
            </p>
            <div class="golf-project-tech">
              <span>OpenStreetMap</span>
              <span>Overpass API</span>
              <span>PeerSocket</span>
              <span>Local backup data</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="golf-project-row">
          <h2>03 — On the course</h2>
          <div class="golf-project-row__body">
            <p>
              During play, the watch’s GPS updates the player’s position and distances to the green and bunkers. A Haversine formula calculates geographic distances from GPS coordinates. When a hole map is available, the position marker is overlaid on its image.
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li>Select the club in use with on-screen controls or the watch’s physical buttons.</li>
              <li>Record each shot with its position and selected club.</li>
              <li>Move between holes while keeping the round’s score.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="golf-project-row">
          <h2>04 — Sync &amp; summary</h2>
          <div class="golf-project-row__body">
            <p>
              At the end of a round, the watch sends a summary to the phone. The phone can send scores as a JSON payload via an HTTP POST request to a personal webhook: course, date, total strokes, and hole-by-hole details.
            </p>
            <p>
              Development accounts for the constraints of a connected watch: a 454 × 454 pixel round display, embedded execution, and Bluetooth communication with the companion app.
            </p>
            <div class="golf-project-tech">
              <span>Zepp OS 1.0</span>
              <span>GPS</span>
              <span>Haversine</span>
              <span>HTTP / JSON</span>
              <span>Webhook</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <div class="golf-project-footer">
          <p>A personal project exploring embedded GPS, open mapping, and sports tracking in real-world conditions.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/b-cb/Golf-Traker" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            View the project on GitHub
            <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </ProjectSection>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .golf-project-content {
    width: min(100%, 74rem);
    margin-inline: auto;
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .golf-project-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(12rem, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 2.2fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 6rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .golf-project-row h2 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    line-height: 1.6;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .golf-project-row__body {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .golf-project-row__body p,
  .golf-project-footer p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .golf-project-row__body ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .golf-project-row__body li::marker {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .golf-project-tech {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.6rem 1.25rem;
    padding-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .golf-project-footer {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 2rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 300;
  }

  .golf-project-footer a {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--footer-link-border);
    border-radius: 0.6rem;
    background: var(--footer-link-bg);
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    color: var(--footer-link-text);
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    transition: border-color 180ms ease, color 180ms ease;
  }

  .golf-project-footer a:hover {
    border-color: var(--footer-link-hover-border);
    color: var(--footer-link-hover-text);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .golf-project-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.25rem;
    }

    .golf-project-footer {
      align-items: flex-start;
      flex-direction: column;
    }
  }
</style>
